and I have been into it.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:17.600
But I just wanna thank you so much

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:20.130
because I started in
late night as a writer,

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.070
and I remember what I
could and couldn't get on

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:25.080
just in terms of jokes out
of like Letterman's mouth.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.374
And I just never even
thought that late night,

00:11:28.374 --> 00:11:30.490
doing a five minute set on late night

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:34.370
would even be something I
would ever be able to do

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:35.850
with the type of comedy that I do.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:38.500
So to your credit and not just me,

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.150
like all the comics that you
book I think are really cool.

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:44.650
And I don't feel out of
them in other places.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:46.290
I mean until they're on your show

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:47.770
and then other people hook into it,

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:51.720
but you do take chances
at risks on comedians.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:53.780
I do get emotional sometimes,

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:56.001
watching comics perform on stage

00:11:56.001 --> 00:11:57.790
and seeing how well it can go.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:58.850
It's the most fun.

00:11:58.850 --> 00:12:02.386
And thank you so much for taking
a chance on an unknown kid.

00:12:02.386 --> 00:12:05.053
(both laughing)

